Subject: corelib: qresource must not call mremap, which wasi-libc only declares

WHAT / WHY

  src/corelib/io/qresource.cpp
      wasi-libc's <sys/mman.h> declares mremap() and defines MREMAP_MAYMOVE,
      MREMAP_FIXED and MREMAP_DONTUNMAP, but NO wasi-sdk library defines the
      symbol (verified with llvm-nm over libc.a, librt.a and every
      libwasi-emulated-*). Qt's own guard is
      `#if defined(MREMAP_MAYMOVE) && defined(MREMAP_DONTUNMAP)`, which those
      macros satisfy -- so QtCore compiles clean and the failure lands at
      APPLICATION link time as "undefined symbol: mremap", from
      qresource.cpp.obj, in a build that has nothing to do with resources.

      `#undef`ing the two macros for Q_OS_WASI selects the fall-through in
      QResourceFileEnginePrivate::mapUncompressed_sys(), which leaves ptr null
      and returns false. The caller (load()) then decompresses into heap memory
      via resource.uncompressedData(). A zero-copy optimisation is lost; there
      is no behavioural change.

  This is the same class of bug as the flock() hunk in 0005 and the eventfd()
  hunk in 0003, and it is the one that makes wasi-libc genuinely nasty to port
  to: THE HEADERS ARE NOT A CONTRACT. __has_include and `#ifdef SOME_FLAG`
  both lie, and every one of these three passed configure, passed the whole
  qtbase build, and only surfaced when a real application was linked. Anything
  added to this port later should be link-tested against a real executable,
  not just compiled.

UPSTREAM
  yes. A guard on a function the platform does not provide, with an existing
  fallback path already in the file.

---
diff --git a/src/corelib/io/qresource.cpp b/src/corelib/io/qresource.cpp
index 82e275e..f3e86d0 100644
--- a/src/corelib/io/qresource.cpp
+++ b/src/corelib/io/qresource.cpp
@@ -42,6 +42,19 @@
 #  elif defined(Q_OS_DARWIN)
 #    include <mach/mach.h>
 #    include <mach/vm_map.h>
+#  elif defined(Q_OS_WASI)
+// wasi-libc's <sys/mman.h> declares mremap() and defines MREMAP_MAYMOVE,
+// MREMAP_FIXED and MREMAP_DONTUNMAP, but NO wasi-sdk library defines the
+// symbol. Left alone, `#if defined(MREMAP_MAYMOVE) && defined(MREMAP_DONTUNMAP)`
+// in mapUncompressed_sys() below is satisfied, QtCore compiles, and an
+// APPLICATION link later fails with "undefined symbol: mremap".
+//
+// Undefining them selects the fall-through in mapUncompressed_sys(), which
+// leaves ptr null, returns false, and makes the caller decompress into heap
+// memory via resource.uncompressedData() instead. That is a
+// zero-copy-optimisation lost, not a behaviour change.
+#    undef MREMAP_MAYMOVE
+#    undef MREMAP_DONTUNMAP
 #  endif
 #endif
 #ifdef Q_OS_WIN
